          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "Laid-off Oracle workers denied better severance as remote classification strips WARN Act rights",
            "articleSection": "Job Evolution",
            "abstract": "Laid-off Oracle employees who attempted to negotiate improved severance packages were rebuffed by the company, which also classified many of them as remote workers — a designation that can disqualify them from WARN Act protections requiring 60 days' advance notice of mass layoffs. The situation highlights a legal grey area that tech companies may increasingly exploit as AI-driven restructuring accelerates. Workers' advocates say the remote-classification tactic effectively strips a meaningful safety net from employees at one of the world's largest enterprise software firms.",
            "url": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/08/laid-off-oracle-workers-tried-to-negotiate-better-severance-oracle-said-no/",
            "publisher": {
              "@type": "NewsMediaOrganization",
              "name": "The AI Chronicle",
              "url": "https://theaichronicle.com",
              "logo": {
